Micro -Mobility data provides above refers to motocycles while HD Trucks were categorized in 'Other'.

Private vehicles and taxis were jointly accounted for as 11%. The data was obtained from lamata and can be accessed via the link below;

https://transformative-mobility.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/TUMI-winner_City-profile-and-story_Lagos-5AhN63.pdf

The analysis is for Mumbai Metropolitan Region (MMR). - https://infralive.com/web/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/Comprehensive-Transport-Study-for-Mumbai-Metropolitan-Region.pdf

The salient findings based on main mode trips are summarized below:
a) The major transportation mode in MMR (about 47%) was noted to be the active modes i.e. walking/cycling for various trip purposes while the rest of the modes are train, bus, metro rail or auto rickshaws. A marginal (11.5%), use of private mode of transport is observed. The
various mode shares without the active modes;
b) Local train (suburban trains) is the major mode of transportation amongst mechanized modes in MMR which transport about 43.2% commuters;
c) Over 16.4% of the commuters use bus as their main mode of transportation and also a significant trips are made by Metro, rickshaws, cars and two wheelers as well.
